cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research codebase or mathematical methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "spatial-justice-lab: Quantifying Spatial (In)Justice With Mathematics, Open Data, and Python"
authors:
  - family-names: Saif
    given-names: Monour Hosan
repository-code: "https://github.com/monourhosan/spatial-justice-lab"
abstract: >-
  A computational and applied mathematical framework operationalizing and empirically testing
  neighborhood socioeconomic disadvantage against walking-network accessibility to public amenities.
  Empirically evaluated using U.S. Census Bureau ACS data, City of Chicago open data portals, and
  OpenStreetMap walking graphs. Inspired by Adnan Zillur Morshed (ed.), Spatial (In)Justice: How
  Does It Manifest in the Built Environment? (John Wiley & Sons, 2024/2025, ISBN: 978-1394294664).
license: "MIT"
